@startuml sign-in-with-google
title Verify the Google credential and resolve the CRM account
hide footbox

participant "CRM client" as Client
participant SignInWithGoogleController as Controller
participant SignInWithGoogleHandler as Handler
participant GoogleSignInTokenVerifier as Verifier
participant LoginSessionIssuer as Session
database "SQL Server" as Database

Client -> Controller: POST /api/auth/google/sign-in\n{idToken, useNativeSession?}
Controller -> Handler: Send SignInWithGoogleCommand with request metadata\nvia MediatR
Handler -> Verifier: VerifyAsync(idToken)
Verifier -> Verifier: Read configured ClientId\nVerify signature, audience, issuer and expiry\nExtract sub, nonce and verified email
break Token is invalid or verification is unavailable
    Verifier --> Handler: Verification exception
    Controller --> Client: 401 or 503 ProblemDetails
end
Verifier --> Handler: VerifiedGoogleSignInIdentity
Handler -> Database: Begin transaction\nDelete challenge with signed nonce and valid expiry
Database --> Handler: Affected row count
break No matching unexpired challenge
    Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
    Controller --> Client: 401 Auth.InvalidGoogleSignIn
end
Handler -> Database: Read link by Google subject\nLoad CRM account with roles
Database --> Handler: Linked CRM account or no match
alt A CRM account is linked
    break Linked account is inactive
        Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
        Controller --> Client: 403 Auth.InactiveAccount.
    end
    Handler -> Session: Issue(account, request metadata)
    Session --> Handler: CRM JWT and refresh token\nRefresh token hash staged for save
else Google subject is unlinked
    break Verified email is missing or invalid
        Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
        Controller --> Client: 401 Auth.GoogleVerifiedEmailRequired
    end
    Handler -> Database: Look up CRM account by verified email
    Database --> Handler: CRM account ID and status, or no match
    break Email belongs to an inactive CRM account
        Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
        Controller --> Client: 403 Auth.InactiveAccount.
    end
    Handler -> Database: Delete expired continuations
    Handler -> Handler: Generate continuation token and SHA-256 hash\nSet expiry to now + 5 minutes
    Handler -> Handler: Stage hash, subject, email and expiry\nStore CRM account ID for linking, null for registration
end
Handler -> Database: SaveChangesAsync and commit
Database --> Handler: Transaction committed
Handler --> Controller: SignedIn(session) or Continue(RequiresLink, token, expiry)
alt SignedIn
    opt Browser session
        Controller -> Controller: Append refresh cookie with LoginRefreshTokenCookie
    end
    Controller --> Client: 200 signedIn, access token and expiry\nNative mode also includes refresh fields in JSON
else Continue
    Controller --> Client: 200 linkRequired or registrationRequired\ncontinuationToken and continuationExpiresAtUtc\nverified email for linkRequired
end
@enduml
